<mxfile host="app.diagrams.net"><diagram name="Data Model" id="job-data"><mxGraphModel dx="1900" dy="1300" grid="1" gridSize="10" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1900" pageHeight="1300" background="#ffffff"><root><mxCell id="0"/><mxCell id="1" parent="0"/>
<mxCell id="t" value="JOB SCHEDULER - Data Model (Cassandra Time-Series + Redis ZSET Queue + Heartbeat Keys + Leader Election)" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;fontSize=20;fontStyle=1;fontColor=#1a237e" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="60" y="20" width="1780" height="35" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

<mxCell id="cassTitle" value="CASSANDRA SCHEMAS (Source of Truth)" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=#7b1fa2;fillColor=#f3e5f5;align=left;fontSize=14;fontStyle=1;rounded=1" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="60" y="80" width="850" height="30" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

<mxCell id="jobsTable" value="jobs table (job definitions)&#10;&#10;PRIMARY KEY: job_id&#10;INDEX: next_run_at (for Scheduler queries)&#10;&#10;┌──────────────────┬─────────────────┬────────────────────────────────────┐&#10;│ Column           │ Type            │ Description                        │&#10;├──────────────────┼─────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────┤&#10;│ job_id           │ UUID            │ PK, unique identifier              │&#10;│ name             │ VARCHAR         │ Human-readable job name            │&#10;│ cron_expr        │ VARCHAR         │ '0 2 * * *' (null for one-time)    │&#10;│ job_type         │ ENUM            │ CRON | ONE_TIME | DEPENDENT         │&#10;│ payload          │ TEXT            │ JSON or S3 key (s3://bucket/key)   │&#10;│ max_retries      │ INT             │ Default 3, then DEAD_LETTER        │&#10;│ timeout_seconds  │ INT             │ Kill job after N seconds           │&#10;│ status           │ ENUM            │ ACTIVE | PAUSED | DELETED          │&#10;│ next_run_at      │ TIMESTAMP       │ Unix timestamp, indexed            │&#10;│ created_at       │ TIMESTAMP       │ Job creation timestamp             │&#10;│ updated_at       │ TIMESTAMP       │ Last modification                  │&#10;└──────────────────┴─────────────────┴────────────────────────────────────┘&#10;&#10;WHY next_run_at index: Scheduler queries SELECT * FROM jobs WHERE next_run_at &lt; now()+60s AND status='ACTIVE'. Without index, full table scan.&#10;WHY TEXT for payload: Job payload can be JSON {report_type: 'sales'} or S3 key s3://jobs/42.json if &gt; 64KB." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f3e5f5;strokeColor=#7b1fa2;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=10;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8;fontFamily=Courier New" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="60" y="120" width="850" height="300" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

<mxCell id="execTable" value="job_executions table (execution history, time-series)&#10;&#10;PRIMARY KEY: (job_id, execution_id)  -- job_id partition, execution_id clustering&#10;CLUSTERING ORDER: execution_id DESC  -- newest first&#10;TTL: 90 days (auto-expire old executions)&#10;&#10;┌──────────────────┬─────────────────┬────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐&#10;│ Column           │ Type            │ Description                                        │&#10;├──────────────────┼─────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤&#10;│ job_id           │ UUID            │ Partition key (all runs for one job co-located)    │&#10;│ execution_id     │ TIMEUUID        │ Clustering key, time-ordered UUID (newest first)   │&#10;│ worker_id        │ VARCHAR         │ Pod/node that executed (e.g., worker-node-07)      │&#10;│ status           │ ENUM            │ SCHEDULED | ENQUEUED | RUNNING | SUCCESS | FAILED │&#10;│                  │                 │ TIMEOUT | CANCELLED | DEAD_LETTER                 │&#10;│ started_at       │ TIMESTAMP       │ Execution start time                               │&#10;│ finished_at      │ TIMESTAMP       │ Execution end time (null if RUNNING)               │&#10;│ retry_count      │ INT             │ Attempt number (0, 1, 2, 3...)                     │&#10;│ error            │ TEXT            │ Error message if FAILED / TIMEOUT                  │&#10;│ output_s3_key    │ VARCHAR         │ S3 key for large outputs (reports, logs)           │&#10;└──────────────────┴─────────────────┴────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘&#10;&#10;WHY time-series partitioning: All executions for job_id=X stored on same Cassandra node. Query SELECT * FROM job_executions WHERE job_id=X ORDER BY execution_id DESC LIMIT 20 is single-partition read, fast.&#10;WHY TIMEUUID: Embeds timestamp in UUID, gives natural ordering, no need for separate created_at column.&#10;WHY TTL 90 days: High-frequency job (1000 runs/day) = 90K rows per job_id partition. TTL auto-deletes old rows without manual cleanup." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f3e5f5;strokeColor=#7b1fa2;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=10;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8;fontFamily=Courier New" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="60" y="440" width="850" height="320" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

<mxCell id="runningTable" value="running_jobs table (Monitor Service index)&#10;&#10;PRIMARY KEY: (shard_date, job_id)  -- partition by date, clustering by job_id&#10;&#10;┌──────────────────┬─────────────────┬────────────────────────────────────┐&#10;│ Column           │ Type            │ Description                        │&#10;├──────────────────┼─────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────┤&#10;│ shard_date       │ DATE            │ Partition key (e.g., 2026-08-21)   │&#10;│ job_id           │ UUID            │ Clustering key                     │&#10;│ execution_id     │ TIMEUUID        │ Current execution ID               │&#10;│ worker_id        │ VARCHAR         │ Which worker owns this job         │&#10;│ started_at       │ TIMESTAMP       │ When job started RUNNING           │&#10;└──────────────────┴─────────────────┴────────────────────────────────────┘&#10;&#10;Worker behavior:&#10;  On RUNNING:  INSERT INTO running_jobs&#10;  On SUCCESS:  DELETE FROM running_jobs WHERE shard_date=today AND job_id=X&#10;  On FAILED:   DELETE FROM running_jobs WHERE shard_date=today AND job_id=X&#10;&#10;Monitor query:&#10;  SELECT * FROM running_jobs WHERE shard_date = '2026-08-21'&#10;  For each row: GET job_heartbeat:{job_id} from Redis&#10;  If heartbeat nil (TTL expired) → job stuck → re-enqueue&#10;&#10;WHY shard_date partition: Avoids full table scan. Monitor only scans today's partition (~10K concurrent jobs at peak). Old dates auto-pruned by daily DELETE." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f3e5f5;strokeColor=#7b1fa2;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=10;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8;fontFamily=Courier New" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="60" y="780" width="850" height="280" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

<mxCell id="redisTitle" value="REDIS KEY SPACE (Ephemeral Queue + State)" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=#f57f17;fillColor=#fff9c4;align=left;fontSize=14;fontStyle=1;rounded=1" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="970" y="80" width="870" height="30" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

<mxCell id="redisQueue" value="job_queue (Sorted Set / ZSET) — Time-based Priority Queue&#10;&#10;Data structure: ZSET&#10;Key: job_queue&#10;Member: job_id (UUID string)&#10;Score: next_run_unix_timestamp (float)&#10;&#10;Commands:&#10;  ZADD job_queue 1724202000 'a7f3c891-4b2e-4d8f-9c1a-3e5f7b9d2a4c'&#10;  ZPOPMIN job_queue 1  →  Atomically removes and returns lowest-score member&#10;  ZRANGEBYSCORE job_queue 0 1724202060  →  All jobs due in next 60 seconds&#10;  ZCARD job_queue  →  Total jobs in queue&#10;&#10;Example queue state:&#10;┌──────────────────┬────────────────────────────────────────┐&#10;│ Score (unix ts)  │ Member (job_id)                        │&#10;├──────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────┤&#10;│ 1724198400       │ abc-123 (due at 2026-08-21 02:00:00)   │&#10;│ 1724198401       │ def-456 (due at 2026-08-21 02:00:01)   │&#10;│ 1724198460       │ ghi-789 (due at 2026-08-21 02:01:00)   │&#10;│ 1724202000       │ jkl-012 (due at 2026-08-21 03:00:00)   │&#10;└──────────────────┴────────────────────────────────────────┘&#10;&#10;WHY ZPOPMIN: Atomic. Two workers calling ZPOPMIN simultaneously each get a different member. Redis guarantees no double-pop.&#10;WHY sorted by timestamp: Workers always grab the earliest-due job first. Natural time-based priority.&#10;NOT Kafka: Kafka is FIFO. Cannot query 'all jobs due NOW' efficiently. ZRANGEBYSCORE answers this in O(log N)." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff9c4;strokeColor=#f57f17;strokeWidth=3;fontSize=10;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8;fontFamily=Courier New" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="970" y="120" width="870" height="290" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

<mxCell id="redisHeartbeat" value="job_heartbeat:{job_id} (String with TTL) — Worker Liveness Detection&#10;&#10;Key pattern: job_heartbeat:{job_id}&#10;Value: worker_id (which worker owns this job)&#10;TTL: 90 seconds (auto-expires if worker dies)&#10;&#10;Worker behavior:&#10;  On job start:    SET job_heartbeat:abc-123 'worker-node-07' EX 90&#10;  Every 30 seconds: SETEX job_heartbeat:abc-123 'worker-node-07' EX 90  (renew)&#10;  On job end:      DEL job_heartbeat:abc-123  (cleanup)&#10;&#10;Monitor Service check:&#10;  GET job_heartbeat:abc-123&#10;  If nil (key expired) → worker died → mark FAILED → re-enqueue&#10;  If exists → worker alive → do nothing&#10;&#10;Example keys:&#10;  job_heartbeat:a7f3c891  →  'worker-node-04'  (TTL: 67 seconds remaining)&#10;  job_heartbeat:def-456   →  'worker-node-07'  (TTL: 42 seconds remaining)&#10;&#10;WHY TTL 90s: Worker renews every 30s. Missed 3 heartbeats (90s) means worker is dead. Too low (30s) → false positives from GC pauses.&#10;WHY Redis not Cassandra: TTL auto-cleanup is native in Redis. Cassandra TTL is less precise and requires compaction." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff9c4;strokeColor=#f57f17;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=10;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8;fontFamily=Courier New" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="970" y="430" width="870" height="260" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

<mxCell id="redisLeader" value="scheduler_leader (String with TTL) — Leader Election&#10;&#10;Key: scheduler_leader&#10;Value: scheduler instance id (e.g., 'scheduler-node-02')&#10;TTL: 30 seconds&#10;&#10;Leader election protocol:&#10;  SET scheduler_leader 'my-instance-id' NX EX 30&#10;  If success (1) → I am the leader, start scheduling&#10;  If failure (0) → Another instance is leader, I am standby&#10;  Leader renews every 15 seconds: SET scheduler_leader 'my-instance-id' XX EX 30&#10;  If leader dies → TTL expires → next instance's NX wins → new leader elected&#10;&#10;Failover timeline:&#10;  t=0s:   Leader-A holds key (TTL 30s), renews at t=15s&#10;  t=10s:  Leader-A crashes (no more renewal)&#10;  t=30s:  Key expires&#10;  t=31s:  Standby-B's SETNX wins → Standby-B becomes leader&#10;  Gap:    1 second (no scheduling between t=30 and t=31)&#10;&#10;WHY leader election: Without it, all 10 Scheduler instances would ZADD same job to Redis → 10 duplicate enqueues → job runs 10 times.&#10;WHY 30s TTL: Balance between fast failover (low TTL) and avoiding split-brain from network hiccups (high TTL)." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff9c4;strokeColor=#f57f17;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=10;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8;fontFamily=Courier New" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="970" y="710" width="870" height="260" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

<mxCell id="redisLock" value="job_executing:{job_id} (String with TTL) — Distributed Lock (Exactly-Once Jobs)&#10;&#10;Key pattern: job_executing:{job_id}&#10;Value: execution_id (UUID for this run)&#10;TTL: timeout_seconds + 60 (buffer for cleanup)&#10;&#10;Usage (for non-idempotent jobs only):&#10;  Before execute: SET job_executing:abc-123 'exec-uuid-xyz' NX EX 1860&#10;  If success (1) → I hold the lock, proceed with execution&#10;  If failure (0) → Another worker is executing, skip this job&#10;  On job end:     DEL job_executing:abc-123  (release lock early)&#10;&#10;Crash scenario:&#10;  Worker A acquires lock, crashes mid-job&#10;  Lock TTL expires after timeout_seconds + 60&#10;  Monitor re-enqueues job&#10;  Worker B's SETNX wins → Worker B executes&#10;  Worker A (if recovers) tries DEL → no-op (key already gone)&#10;&#10;WHY exactly-once vs at-least-once:&#10;  Idempotent jobs (99% of cases): skip distributed lock, use at-least-once. Job checks 'already processed?' internally.&#10;  Non-idempotent jobs (legacy payment APIs, third-party webhooks): must use distributed lock to guarantee single execution." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff9c4;strokeColor=#f57f17;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=10;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8;fontFamily=Courier New" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="970" y="990" width="870" height="270" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

<mxCell id="failures" value="FAILURE SCENARIOS&#10;&#10;1. Worker crash mid-execution:&#10;   Detection: Heartbeat expires (90s TTL, no renewal)&#10;   Recovery: Monitor scans running_jobs, checks Redis heartbeat, marks FAILED, re-enqueues with new execution_id, exponential backoff (1s → 2s → 4s → 8s)&#10;   Data: Both execution_ids exist in job_executions (original FAILED, retry SUCCESS). Execution history preserved.&#10;&#10;2. Scheduler leader crash:&#10;   Detection: scheduler_leader key TTL expires (30s)&#10;   Recovery: Standby Scheduler's SETNX wins, becomes new leader within 1 second&#10;   Gap: 0-30s no scheduling (jobs may start late). Tolerable for batch jobs. Next cycle (t=31s) enqueues missed jobs.&#10;&#10;3. Redis crash:&#10;   Impact: job_queue (ZSET) lost. Workers cannot pop jobs. New jobs cannot be enqueued.&#10;   Recovery: Scheduler reads Cassandra, rebuilds queue (ZADD all jobs WHERE next_run_at &lt; now+60s). In-flight jobs (RUNNING in Cassandra) re-enqueued by Monitor.&#10;   Data loss: Enqueued jobs (not yet RUNNING) lost. Scheduler re-enqueues from source of truth (Cassandra) on next cycle.&#10;&#10;4. Cassandra partition:&#10;   Impact: Cannot read job definitions. Workers starve (ZPOPMIN succeeds but SELECT jobs fails). Scheduler cannot enqueue new jobs.&#10;   Recovery: Retry with exponential backoff. Alert ops. Workers idle until Cassandra recovers. No data loss (Cassandra is source of truth, replicated).&#10;&#10;5. Thundering herd (10K jobs midnight):&#10;   Prevention: Deterministic jitter: next_run = cron_time + (hash(job_id) % 300). Spreads jobs over 5 minutes (33 jobs/sec). Workers drain steadily.&#10;   Monitoring: Track queue_length (ZCARD job_queue). Alert if &gt; 50K jobs (indicates workers falling behind).&#10;&#10;6. Job exceeds max_retries (3):&#10;   Action: status = DEAD_LETTER. Alert ops team (PagerDuty / Slack). No more automatic retries.&#10;   Debugging: GET /jobs/{id}/executions/{execution_id}/logs → S3 logs. Check error field in job_executions. Fix payload or code bug.&#10;   Recovery: POST /jobs/{id}/retry (creates new execution with retry_count=0) or DELETE + recreate job." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffebee;strokeColor=#c62828;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=10;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8;fontFamily=Courier New" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="60" y="1090" width="1780" height="160" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

</root></mxGraphModel></diagram></mxfile>
